/*
A demonstration program for GCBASIC.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 mTouch capacitive touch, eight buttons, on the Microchip mTouch CVD Evaluation Board (PIC16F1937, assembly
 02-02091) with the 8-button sensor board (02-02094), implemented as Microchip's mTouch Framework v2.3
 (mTouch SW Package 1.43, project "02-02091-R3 CVD Eval Board\8 Buttons") does it, in plain GCBASIC.
 The touch sensing is in the library mTouchCVD_8Buttons.h, shared with the serial version
 GCBASIC_mTouch_Framework_CVD_8Buttons_Serial_16F1937.gcb.
 See GCBASIC_mTouch_Framework_CVD_8Buttons_explained.md for how it works.

 Board
  o PIC16F1937 at 32 MHz (internal oscillator with the PLL)
  o Sensors 0-7 on AN0-AN7: RA0, RA1, RA2, RA3, RA5, RE0, RE1, RE2
  o LEDs for sensors 0-7 (on when low): RC2, RC1, RC0, RA7, RA6, RA4, RD7, RD6

 On startup all eight LEDs light for one second. Then each LED lights while its button is touched.

 Touch sensing: a two-phase differential capacitive voltage divider (CVD) reading per sensor. With several
 sensors the framework charges the ADC's hold capacitor (CHOLD) through another sensor's pin, the reference
 (sensor n uses sensor n - 1, sensor 0 uses sensor 7), not through the pad itself.
    Scan A: the reference is driven high and CHOLD connected to it (CHOLD charges high); the sensor, driven low
            until now, is made an input and CHOLD connected to it: they share their charge, settle, and the ADC
            converts. Then the sensor is driven high.
    Scan B: the same with the levels swapped (CHOLD low, sensor high). Then the sensor is driven low again.
    Reading = B - A + 1024, as the framework: a touch raises it. Noise common to both scans cancels.
    A random delay before each reading (jitter) keeps the readings from locking on to periodic noise.
    Each reading moves a slew-limited value by at most 10 (the framework's decimation filter); eight of those
    are summed. All eight sensors are scanned every 10 ms (millis).
    Power-up: the baseline follows the sum for 0.3 s. Then press when the sum is TOUCH_PRESS above the baseline,
    release below TOUCH_RELEASE (hysteresis); the baseline follows slowly (1/16 every 10th scan) only while
    released. A press held for 10 s (something left on the pad) starts the power-up learning again.

 The one-sensor version of the same method is GCBASIC_mTouch_Framework_CVD_Curiosity_board_16F1619.gcb.

@author    Evan R. Venn
@license   GPL
@version   1.01

1.00  New implementation for the mTouch CVD Evaluation Board with the 8-button sensor board, from the mTouch
      Framework v2.3 8 Buttons project: reference sensor charging, charge and settling delays (1 us each), jitter,
      decimation step 10, power-up learning for 30 scans, baseline every 10th scan, press time-out 10 s
1.01  The touch sensing moved to the shared library mTouchCVD_8Buttons.h (unchanged)
*/


// ---- Configuration
#CHIP 16F1937, 32
#CONFIG MCLRE_OFF                       // as Microchip's firmware for the board

#OPTION Explicit

#option IncludePath "C:\GCstudio\gcbasic\AdditionalLibraries;GCBASICLibraries"
#include <mTouchCVD_8Buttons.h>

// ---- LEDs, one per sensor, on when low
#DEFINE LED0 PORTC.2
#DEFINE LED1 PORTC.1
#DEFINE LED2 PORTC.0
#DEFINE LED3 PORTA.7
#DEFINE LED4 PORTA.6
#DEFINE LED5 PORTA.4
#DEFINE LED6 PORTD.7
#DEFINE LED7 PORTD.6
Dir LED0 Out
Dir LED1 Out
Dir LED2 Out
Dir LED3 Out
Dir LED4 Out
Dir LED5 Out
Dir LED6 Out
Dir LED7 Out

// ---- Main
// LEDs off, the sensor pins driven low
LedsOff
TouchInit

// Start-up: all LEDs on for one second while the pads settle. Keep off the pads until 0.3 s after they go out:
// the scans then set the baselines
LedsOn
Wait 1 s
LedsOff
TouchStart

Do Forever
    TouchService
    If TouchNewScan = 1 Then
        TouchShowLeds
    End If
Loop

Sub LedsOn
    // Every LED on
    LED0 = 0
    LED1 = 0
    LED2 = 0
    LED3 = 0
    LED4 = 0
    LED5 = 0
    LED6 = 0
    LED7 = 0
End Sub

Sub LedsOff
    // Every LED off
    LED0 = 1
    LED1 = 1
    LED2 = 1
    LED3 = 1
    LED4 = 1
    LED5 = 1
    LED6 = 1
    LED7 = 1
End Sub

Sub TouchShowLeds
    // Each LED on (low) while its sensor is pressed
    LED0 = 1
    If TouchState(0) = 2 Then LED0 = 0
    LED1 = 1
    If TouchState(1) = 2 Then LED1 = 0
    LED2 = 1
    If TouchState(2) = 2 Then LED2 = 0
    LED3 = 1
    If TouchState(3) = 2 Then LED3 = 0
    LED4 = 1
    If TouchState(4) = 2 Then LED4 = 0
    LED5 = 1
    If TouchState(5) = 2 Then LED5 = 0
    LED6 = 1
    If TouchState(6) = 2 Then LED6 = 0
    LED7 = 1
    If TouchState(7) = 2 Then LED7 = 0
End Sub
